From 8cdb506a9244387f775c725cd097061fd2c1b76b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 16:47:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: AMD FSR 3.1 as the temporal upscaler too
 (PS3RECOMP_TEMPORAL=fsr3)

rsx_vk_fsr3.cpp drives the FidelityFX SDK's FSR 3 upscaler through its
VK backend, built into a static library outside the repository
(PS3RECOMP_FFX_DIR; a stub without it). The backend's device functions
reach it through a lookup that gives core functions for *2KHR names and
stand-ins for the debug-label and marker extensions it calls unchecked;
the instance functions it calls directly go through the runtime's
loader. The caller keeps FSR 3.1's three shared images.

The motion pass also writes the depth as an R32F image (the first-person
model's where it was drawn, the world's elsewhere), which both
upscalers now take. The device gets the 16-bit and format-less storage
features FSR's shaders declare. PS3RECOMP_UPSCALE_MODE=quality |
balanced | performance | ultra | native picks the mode for either; the
temporal record carries the camera's near, far and vertical FOV.

